            <abstract lang="en">
                <p>Enhanced authentication techniques may include receiving device data of a secondary device by a primary device, transmitting a provision request to an authorization server to request account credentials associated with an account, receiving a provision response from the authorization server comprising encrypted account credentials comprised of a first part and a second part and a shared key associated with the primary device, storing by the primary device the shared key and the first part of the encrypted account credentials, and transmitting the second part of the encrypted account credentials of the secondary device for storage.</p>
